# THIRTY MINUTES ON THE HOME COAST (docs/ROADMAP.md, slice 1): the slice's proof,
# played from the title the way a player starts, with nothing given, no folk and
# no beats pre-landed. Each step of the slice extends it.
#
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/home-coast.tour --scene=title --seed=1
#
# At a fixed frame rate: from step 3 on a machine's tells are waited for, and a
# loaded box's frames let them go by (the keeper's block, as reaper_plating's).
# It may down him on the way to its plate; that is the fight, and it costs him
# hours and a meal, which is why the goal after it is his hunger's until step 4
# stages the fight itself.
#
# 1a THE WAKE (48_wake): a new game starts him under the water in the shallows
# off the spawn beach, the black site in the sea behind him and Maren at the
# water's edge. 01 he breaks the surface; 02 he stands in the surf with his legs,
# from above; 03 the first sight of the Tether; 04 over the shoulder, looking to
# the shore and her.
await title 40
# New game heads the title's list when there is no save to continue; with one,
# continue would, and `await character` below fails rather than play a save.
tap use
await character 8
key move_up
key use
await game 40
await waking 5
wait 0.4
shot 01-he-breaks-the-surface with waking,wake:staged
await woken 10
wait 1.0
shot 02-in-the-surf-from-above with woken,cast:maren
# 1b THE FIRST SIGHT (48_wake, 42_stage): a breath after he stands, the view
# turns once to the far horizon and up the Tether to the Foundry, and holds.
await staging:tether 6
wait 1.2
shot 03-the-first-sight with staging:tether,tether
wait 4.0
tap shoulder
await shoulder 20
wait 1.0
shot 04-in-the-surf-over-the-shoulder with woken,cast:maren,shoulder

# 2 MAREN'S ASK BECOMES THE GOAL (Guide._led, StoryContent.LEAD): he goes to her
# at the water's edge and talks, taking the first reply each time, as a player
# who just keeps talking does, until she gives his first lead; then the goal
# line is her lead in her words, and it points on to the crew's camp.
at cast:maren
await cast:maren 8
wait 0.6
press use
await talking 3
wait 0.4
shot 05-maren-at-the-water with talking,cast:maren
press use
wait 0.5
press use
wait 0.5
press use
wait 0.5
press use
await beat:marens_lead 3
wait 0.5
shot 06-her-lead with talking,beat:marens_lead
press use
wait 2.5
shot 07-the-goal-is-hers with beat:marens_lead

# 3 THE FIRE, THE CHARCOAL, THE PICK (Guide._led: her lead in her words, in the
# order the way in asks: a fire, charcoal, a haft, plate, a pick). Everything is
# taken by hand from the coast round the spawn, nothing given: five takes of
# driftwood (a fire's three, a haft's two, a batch of charcoal's four), two
# stones, and a plate turned out of a tip. From above, as the making is done: at
# eye level the meadow's grass stands round him and no tile of it is open ground.
coast calm
tap shoulder
wait 1.0
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
wait 0.2
shot 08-driftwood-off-the-strand
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near tip
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 20
end
wait 0.2
shot 09-a-plate-turned-out-of-the-tip
ground grass
mark fire
press use 0.1
await fire_asked 2
# The ask is a prompt on the glass; the second press answers it once it is up.
wait 0.6
press use 0.1
await made 4
wait 0.5
shot 10-his-fire-laid with station:fire
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose charcoal
tap use
wait 0.3
choose haft
tap use
await made 3
tap pause
wait 0.4
hour 11
await made 4
wait 0.3
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose pick_made
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
hour 12
await made 4
wait 0.3
tap inventory
wait 0.6
shot 11-a-pick-of-his-own with app:inventory
tap inventory
wait 0.4

# 4 THE TIDE REAPER, NAMED (Guide.edge_line, StoryContent.EDGE, KEEPER_NAMED):
# Hob, who picks the tide past the point, names the yard and its keeper and says
# what bites it; then at the keeper the knife rings off its plate, and the goal
# is the steel edge in Hob's words.
at cast:hob
await cast:hob 8
wait 0.6
press use
await talking 3
wait 0.4
press use
wait 0.5
press use
wait 0.5
press use
await beat:reaper_named 3
wait 0.5
shot 12-hob-names-it with talking,beat:reaper_named
press use
wait 1.0
near keeper
wait 0.6
await sentinel 12
try 8
  walkto mob 6
  await tell 14
  press dodge 0.12
  await sentinel_open 6
  walkto part 2
  tap swing
  await plating 5
end
wait 0.4
shot 13-the-knife-rings-off-it with plating

# 5 THE STEEL (Guide.edge_goal, StoryContent.EDGE): back at his fire the goal is
# the steel edge in Hob's words, then everything it asks, gathered: four charcoal,
# eight stones, a kiln at Low Scar, the knife tempered over a night there. Low
# Scar is the Reaper's region's other village, 205 tiles off Oyster Row, where
# he woke and was seen; a night away is when the plan comes for who saw him.
at mark:fire
wait 1.0
# Fed first, as a player would be: the ring cost him hours and a hungry body's
# goal is its hunger (Guide), not the steel.
# Berries off the bushes on the grass round his fire (mussels come only at low
# tide, and a tour cannot wait on the sea), one at a time and eaten by it, until
# his hunger no longer outranks the steel: a berry puts his last meal an hour and
# a half later, and how far past it the ring has left him is the fight's.
try 10
  near bush
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 8
  at mark:fire
  wait 0.5
  press use 0.1
  wait 1.5
  await goal:kiln_stones 2
end
shot 14-the-goal-asks-for-steel with beat:reaper_named,goal:kiln_stones
# Four charcoal for the temper, from two batches: the pick took one of the first.
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
try 3
  near driftwood
  press use 0.1
  await took 4
end
at mark:fire
wait 0.5
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose charcoal
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
# Forty minutes on the fire, waited out: how late the ring has left the day is
# the fight's, and `hour` only moves within the day.
await made 45
wait 0.5
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose charcoal
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
await made 45
wait 0.3
village 36
wait 1.5
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
try 3
  near boulder,stone_ore
  walk 0,0 0.05
  press use 0.1
  await took 14
end
ground grass
mark kiln
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose kiln
tap use
await station:kiln 20
# The making page stays open after a build; shut, so the frame is the kiln.
tap pause
wait 0.6
shot 15-a-kiln-at-low-scar with station:kiln
tap craft
wait 0.6
choose knife_cemented
tap use
wait 0.3
tap pause
wait 0.4
hour 20
village 36
wait 0.5
press use 0.1
await slept 10
at mark:kiln
wait 0.5
await made 10
wait 0.5
shot 16-steel-in-his-hand with goal:steel_in_hand

# 6 WHO SAW HIM (48_raids, SnatchNight): while he was away at the Reaper and at
# Low Scar, the plan came in the small hours for somebody out of Oyster Row, and
# holds them at the Reaper's region's yard.
await taken 5
at rescue:yard
wait 1.0
await held_here 6
shot 17-the-yard-holding-somebody-from-oyster-row with works,works_lit,works_yard
